{"uncertainty": 0.35, "outcome": "Extended the approved idle testbench into a self-checking coverage testbench (tick_timer_cov_tb.sv). It drives every line of tick_timer.v and every reachable toggle. The platform's coverage.read run over this file and the approved RTL has not happened yet, so I report no coverage numbers.", "artifacts": [{"kind": "coverage_report", "title": "Coverage closure plan and gap analysis for tick_timer (W=16)", "summary": "Serves [requirement:req-33bb46282b]. Design under measurement: tick_timer.v [artifact:prj-4fd2403e98.design-under-test.a1]. It extends the approved idle testbench [artifact:prj-4fd2403e98.testbench.a1]; that testbench's passing run [run:run-0001] (5 checks) never starts the timer. No coverage numbers are reported here; they will come only from the platform's coverage.read run. Stimulus mapped to code: (1) reset values and register read-back for all four addresses cover every rdata case arm. (2) A LOAD write of 0xFFFFFFFF, read back as 0x0000FFFF, toggles all wdata bits 0->1->0 and checks that bits above W are ignored. (3) One-shot mode with LOAD=3 covers the reload on start, the decrement branch, expiry with en cleared, irq with IE set, a STATUS write of 0 that does not clear, and the W1C clear. (4) Periodic mode with LOAD=2 covers the reload on expiry, a clear followed by re-expiry, an expiry and a clear at the same edge (the expiry wins), a CTRL write at the expiry edge (it suppresses the expiry and holds the count), and a stop that holds the count with irq raised. (5) LOAD=0xFFFF started and stopped, then LOAD=0 started, toggles every count and load bit both ways. (6) A reset while running returns every register to zero. Points expected to stay unhit, with the reason: rdata[31:16] is constant zero for W=16 by design (unreachable); unused_wdata is constant 0 by construction (unreachable, a lint sink). Dead code is not claimed as covered. If the requirement's toggle bound counts these bits, it may not be met, and that needs an exclusion decision instead of more stimulus."}], "files": [{"path": "tick_timer_cov_tb.sv", "kind": "testbench", "title": "tick_timer coverage testbench", "summary": "A self-checking SystemVerilog testbench for tick_timer.v [artifact:prj-4fd2403e98.design-under-test.a1]. It extends the approved idle testbench [artifact:prj-4fd2403e98.testbench.a1] with one-shot, periodic, W1C, same-edge, stop and reset-in-flight scenarios and full-width LOAD/COUNT toggles, serving [requirement:req-33bb46282b]. It uses no $fopen, $system, DPI, include, or coverage pragmas. It prints the NIRMAAN-SIM verdict line with the nonce.", "entry": "tick_timer_cov_tb"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["Expected values were derived by hand from the RTL's edge-by-edge behaviour; they have not been simulated by me.", "All lines and branches of tick_timer.v should be reached by the stimulus; this is unverified until the platform's coverage.read run.", "rdata[31:16] and unused_wdata cannot toggle for W=16, so toggle coverage below 100% is expected on those points."], "escalation": null, "notes": "No coverage bounds for line, toggle or branch were given in the four sections, so whether the targets are reached cannot be judged here. If the toggle bound includes the constant rdata[31:16] and unused_wdata points, I need an exclusion decision (category: unreachable) signed off by the designer. Checks are timed so that every register read falls within 5 ns after a clock edge, inside the 10 ns period."}

=== FILE: tick_timer_cov_tb.sv ===
// Coverage testbench for tick_timer.v (W = 16). Extends tick_timer_idle_tb.sv:
// one-shot and periodic counting, expiry, W1C clear, expiry-vs-clear at the
// same edge, CTRL write at the expiry edge, stop/hold, full-width LOAD and
// COUNT toggles, and a reset while running. Every check is self-checking.
`timescale 1ns / 1ps
module tick_timer_cov_tb;
    logic        clk = 1'b0;
    logic        rst_n = 1'b0;
    logic        we = 1'b0;
    logic [1:0]  addr = 2'd0;
    logic [31:0] wdata = 32'd0;
    logic [31:0] rdata;
    logic        irq;
    int checks = 0, errors = 0;
    logic [8*64-1:0] nonce;

    localparam logic [1:0] CTRL = 2'd0, LOAD = 2'd1, COUNT = 2'd2, STATUS = 2'd3;

    tick_timer #(.W(16)) dut (.clk(clk), .rst_n(rst_n), .we(we), .addr(addr), .wdata(wdata), .rdata(rdata), .irq(irq));
    always #5 clk = ~clk;

    // Advance to 1 ns after the next rising edge.
    task automatic tick();
        @(posedge clk);
        #1;
    endtask

    task automatic expect_reg(input logic [1:0] a, input logic [31:0] expected);
        addr = a;
        #1;
        checks++;
        if (rdata !== expected) begin
            errors++;
            $display("ERROR t=%0t addr=%0d rdata=%h expected=%h", $time, a, rdata, expected);
        end
    endtask

    task automatic expect_irq(input logic expected);
        checks++;
        if (irq !== expected) begin
            errors++;
            $display("ERROR t=%0t irq=%b expected=%b", $time, irq, expected);
        end
    endtask

    // One register write, taking effect at the next rising edge.
    task automatic wr(input logic [1:0] a, input logic [31:0] d);
        we = 1'b1; addr = a; wdata = d;
        @(posedge clk); #1;
        we = 1'b0; wdata = 32'd0;
    endtask

    initial begin
        repeat (3) @(posedge clk);
        rst_n = 1'b1;
        tick();

        // Reset values.
        expect_reg(CTRL, 32'd0);
        expect_reg(LOAD, 32'd0);
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd0);
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd0);
        expect_irq(1'b0);

        // LOAD stores only W bits; all wdata bits toggle.
        wr(LOAD, 32'hFFFF_FFFF);
        expect_reg(LOAD, 32'h0000_FFFF);
        wr(LOAD, 32'h0000_0000);
        expect_reg(LOAD, 32'd0);

        // One-shot: LOAD 3, EN|IE.
        wr(LOAD, 32'd3);
        wr(CTRL, 32'h0000_0005);
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd3);
        expect_reg(CTRL, 32'h0000_0005);
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd0);
        expect_irq(1'b0);
        tick();
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd2);
        repeat (5) tick();
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd1);
        expect_reg(CTRL, 32'h0000_0004);   // EN cleared by the one-shot expiry
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd0);
        expect_irq(1'b1);
        wr(STATUS, 32'd0);                  // writing zero does not clear
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd1);
        wr(STATUS, 32'd1);                  // W1C
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd0);
        expect_irq(1'b0);

        // Periodic: LOAD 2, EN|MODE, IE off.
        wr(LOAD, 32'd2);
        wr(CTRL, 32'h0000_0003);            // E0: count <= 2
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd2);
        tick();                             // E1
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd1);
        tick();                             // E2
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd0);
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd0);
        tick();                             // E3: expire, reload
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd1);
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd2);
        expect_reg(CTRL, 32'h0000_0003);
        expect_irq(1'b0);                   // IE off
        wr(STATUS, 32'd1);                  // E4: clear
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd0);
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd1);
        tick();                             // E5
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd0);
        wr(STATUS, 32'd1);                  // E6: expiry wins over clear
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd1);
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd2);
        wr(STATUS, 32'd1);                  // E7: clear
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd0);
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd1);
        tick();                             // E8
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd0);
        wr(CTRL, 32'h0000_0003);            // E9: CTRL write takes the expiry edge
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd0);
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd0);
        expect_reg(CTRL, 32'h0000_0003);
        tick();                             // E10: expire, reload
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd1);
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd2);
        wr(CTRL, 32'h0000_0006);            // E11: stop, MODE|IE, count holds
        expect_reg(CTRL, 32'h0000_0006);
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd2);
        expect_irq(1'b1);
        repeat (3) tick();
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd2);
        wr(STATUS, 32'd1);
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd0);
        expect_irq(1'b0);

        // Full-width COUNT and LOAD toggles.
        wr(CTRL, 32'h0000_0000);
        wr(LOAD, 32'h0000_FFFF);
        wr(CTRL, 32'h0000_0001);            // count <= FFFF
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'h0000_FFFF);
        tick();
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'h0000_FFFE);
        wr(CTRL, 32'h0000_0000);            // stop, hold
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'h0000_FFFE);
        wr(LOAD, 32'h0000_0000);
        expect_reg(LOAD, 32'd0);
        wr(CTRL, 32'h0000_0001);            // count <= 0
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd0);
        tick();                             // one-shot expiry from zero
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd1);
        expect_reg(CTRL, 32'd0);
        wr(STATUS, 32'd1);
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd0);

        // Reset while running.
        wr(LOAD, 32'd5);
        wr(CTRL, 32'h0000_0007);
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd5);
        rst_n = 1'b0;
        tick();
        tick();
        rst_n = 1'b1;
        tick();
        expect_reg(CTRL, 32'd0);
        expect_reg(LOAD, 32'd0);
        expect_reg(COUNT, 32'd0);
        expect_reg(STATUS, 32'd0);
        expect_irq(1'b0);

        if (!$value$plusargs("nirmaan_nonce=%s", nonce)) nonce = "none";
        $display("NIRMAAN-SIM %0s %0d passed, %0d failed", nonce, (checks > errors ? checks - errors : 0), errors);
        $finish;
    end
endmodule
=== END FILE ===
